==English==
{{Wikipedia}}
=== Etymology ===
From Latin ''receptaculum'', from ''recipere'', "to receive", from ''capere'', "to hold"

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
# A [[container]], [[object]] or [[space]] used to contain something : trash receptacles.
# Zoology term for
#:An [[organ]] or [[structure]] that receives a [[secretion]], [[eggs]], [[sperm]], etc.
# Botanical term for 
#:That part of the [[flower]] [[stalk]] ([[peduncle]] or [[pedicel]]) to which the floral parts are attached; also [[torus]].   In the Asteraceae, the end of the [[peduncle]] to which all of the [[florets]] of the flower head are attached.
#(electrical) US -- a contact device installed at an [[outlet]] for the connection of an attachment plug and flexible cord to supply portable equipment or appliances.



